          "filename": "War memorial and All Saints' church - geograph.org.uk - 1222040.jpg",
          "caption": "War memorial and All Saints'  church This is the church as rebuilt after the great fire of Northampton in 1675.\nThe war memorial was designed by Sir Edwin Lutyens, who was also responsible for the Cenotaph in London, and unveiled on 11 November 1926. At the time, the memorial served as the towns remembrance for over 6,000 Northamptonians lost in the First World War but now is the focus of every remembrance ceremony for all subsequent wars.",
